= Smart contract — Simple =

A smart contract is a program that runs under a blockchain or distributed ledger's rules. It can update ledger state when transactions call it. The name does not mean every smart contract is a legal contract.

'''Important boundary:''' smart contract ≠ legal contract by definition.

